(3832557, 542632, 16004, '<td valign="top">ha! i saw this dude last wednesday in covent garden!  freaked me out initially, have to confess.  does he fit the challenge though?  i guess it does in a literal sense (one chap is hidden and is evident from the bit of flesh behind the glove).  i do wish the environment played more of a part of the shot though.  still, there are very nice elements; the partial desatuation makes for a pleasant change, and the main subject is suitably creepy enough.  i do have a slight advantage in that i know the dude moves; i wonder if this is conveyed well enough to the un-initiated?  <br/> <br/>My First Weighted Scoring System ; composition + technical 1.5/3, challenge 0.75/1, post processing results 1.75/2, ooooh factor 2/3, originality 1/1 = 7</td>', 'ha! i saw this dude last wednesday in covent garden!  freaked me out initially, have to confess.  does he fit the challenge though?  i guess it does in a literal sense (one chap is hidden and is evident from the bit of flesh behind the glove).  i do wish the environment played more of a part of the shot though.  still, there are very nice elements; the partial desatuation makes for a pleasant change, and the main subject is suitably creepy enough.  i do have a slight advantage in that i know the dude moves; i wonder if this is conveyed well enough to the un-initiated?   My First Weighted Scoring System ; composition + technical 1.5/3, challenge 0.75/1, post processing results 1.75/2, ooooh factor 2/3, originality 1/1 = 7', '2007-06-25 16:20:55.000000', NULL, 1),
