(3867841, 540929, 49865, '<td valign="top">I think you made the right choice for your challenge entry, as this is the best of the three photos, when compared to the outtakes. Excellent job - it''s subtle, but the person isn''t difficult to find.</td>', 'I think you made the right choice for your challenge entry, as this is the best of the three photos, when compared to the outtakes. Excellent job - it''s subtle, but the person isn''t difficult to find.', '2007-07-04 14:30:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3867846, 541023, 49865, '<td valign="top">I love the forest. This is going straight into my favorites.</td>', 'I love the forest. This is going straight into my favorites.', '2007-07-04 14:31:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3867996, 541108, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>I love the feel here. The dark woods is interesting in itself, but the old car and subtle sepia convey the viewer back in time and make one wonder what might have been. Very well done.<br/> <br/>There is a nice tension here. The obvious focal point is the end of the path; lots of lines (especially the path) lead to it and it''s brightness catches the eye. The car is off to the side, and it''s lines lead to the end of the path as well; so it clearly isn''t the focal point. But it attracts attention because it is so different from the rest of the scene, and because of the kid in the window. But as soon as you look at it, it immediately leads your gaze back to the path. Great composition.<br/> <br/>There''s a bright area to the left of the focal point, not as bright as the end of the path itself, but still bright enough to cause some minor distraction. I think a little judicious burning to tone it down a bit would improve the photo. But that''s minor; this really is a very good photo. I like it very much.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  I love the feel here. The dark woods is interesting in itself, but the old car and subtle sepia convey the viewer back in time and make one wonder what might have been. Very well done. There is a nice tension here. The obvious focal point is the end of the path; lots of lines (especially the path) lead to it and it''s brightness catches the eye. The car is off to the side, and it''s lines lead to the end of the path as well; so it clearly isn''t the focal point. But it attracts attention because it is so different from the rest of the scene, and because of the kid in the window. But as soon as you look at it, it immediately leads your gaze back to the path. Great composition. There''s a bright area to the left of the focal point, not as bright as the end of the path itself, but still bright enough to cause some minor distraction. I think a little judicious burning to tone it down a bit would improve the photo. But that''s minor; this really is a very good photo. I like it very much.', '2007-07-04 15:18:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3868007, 541878, 51802, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>My first impression is that color treatment does not work here.  If you were going for an antique photo look, then maybe a bit more orange and less red would have helped.  Otherwise, I think it would have come out nicely as a simple B&amp;W with no tinting.<br/> <br/>This photo does have a spooky feel too it which helps draw interest.  You also did a great job on your composition, keeping the light over the door behind the column was a good idea.<br/> <br/>This shot meets the challenge well.  It is refreshing to see that the person is actually hidden instead of so small he is hard to notice.<br/> <br/>I think what kept this entry from scoring higher is that there is not much wow factor.  Wow factor is really important if you want to capture someone''s attention when they are voting.  Otherwise they will give you a 5 and move on.</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club!  My first impression is that color treatment does not work here.  If you were going for an antique photo look, then maybe a bit more orange and less red would have helped.  Otherwise, I think it would have come out nicely as a simple B&W with no tinting. This photo does have a spooky feel too it which helps draw interest.  You also did a great job on your composition, keeping the light over the door behind the column was a good idea. This shot meets the challenge well.  It is refreshing to see that the person is actually hidden instead of so small he is hard to notice. I think what kept this entry from scoring higher is that there is not much wow factor.  Wow factor is really important if you want to capture someone''s attention when they are voting.  Otherwise they will give you a 5 and move on.', '2007-07-04 15:23:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3868062, 540929, 22734, '<td valign="top">Glad to see this formidable study walk away with the Blue. The execution with the waldo angled head placement works so fine! Congratulations on your neat accomplishment!</td>', 'Glad to see this formidable study walk away with the Blue. The execution with the waldo angled head placement works so fine! Congratulations on your neat accomplishment!', '2007-07-04 15:46:02.000000', NULL, 0),
