(3868178, 542880, 67697, '<td valign="top">Well deb, once again, your photo not accepted by the DPC brethren.  I do think this should have at least finished in the 5 range.  I did give this one a 5 in the challenge because for me there wasn''t much pulling me in.  I think that once the viewer sees the red, they just kind of stop looking (because of the challenge theme), and are ready to move on.  The other thing I have been learning is that the time of day can greatly affect the mood of the photo (i.e. the lighting).  But, yeah, the guy was there at the time, so what are you gonna do?  I think it was composed well with Waldo being there in the right.<br/> <br/>Never give up woman!</td>', 'Well deb, once again, your photo not accepted by the DPC brethren.  I do think this should have at least finished in the 5 range.  I did give this one a 5 in the challenge because for me there wasn''t much pulling me in.  I think that once the viewer sees the red, they just kind of stop looking (because of the challenge theme), and are ready to move on.  The other thing I have been learning is that the time of day can greatly affect the mood of the photo (i.e. the lighting).  But, yeah, the guy was there at the time, so what are you gonna do?  I think it was composed well with Waldo being there in the right. Never give up woman!', '2007-07-04 16:13:34.000000', NULL, 0),
